# UnEncrypted Chat Server – Version 1.2.0
==========================================
Released January 2026 - The-R34per


# Overview
This update represents a major refactor and modernization of the original UnEncrypted Chat Server. 
The entire codebase has been cleaned, reorganized, documented, and expanded with new features, improved GUI behavior, better server control, and a more robust client/server communication model.


# Added
=========
-> New ChatServer class  
Replaced the old ExampleChatServer with a fully‑refactored ChatServer class featuring clearer structure, improved naming, and professional documentation.

-> Admin Kick System (GUI + Client)
Server GUI now includes a Kick User button with a selection dialog.
Clients can kick users using /kickuser with the admin password (default admin password is "admin123").
Server broadcasts kick notifications to all users.

-> Admin password prompt added on the client side.

-> Server Shutdown Broadcast
Server sends a SERVER_SHUTDOWN command to all clients.
Clients display a shutdown countdown window before exiting.

-> Dynamic Host + Port Selection
Server GUI prompts for IP and port at startup.
Client GUI prompts for host, port, and display name.

-> Improved Client Disconnect Handling
Server logs disconnects with formatted output.

-> Client receives a message when kicked or disconnected.

-> ASCII Art Banner in Server GUI
Added a centered banner with version info and author credit.

-> Log Saving System
Server GUI now includes a Save Log button.
Saves full server log to a user‑selected file.


# Changed
===========

-> Complete rewrite of server start logic
Replaced new ServerSocket(port) with explicit binding using InetSocketAddress(host, port).

-> Renamed and reorganized classes
Updated all references across the project.

-> Improved GUI layout and styling
Monospaced fonts for logs and user lists.
Better spacing, borders, and panel organization.

-> Client message handling refactored
Cleaner separation of commands (/userList, /kickuser, shutdown, etc.).
Removed duplicate logic and improved readability.

-> Threading improvements
Server runs on a background thread to avoid freezing the GUI.
Client reader thread marked as daemon.

-> Enhanced logging
More consistent formatting.
Clear separators for connect/disconnect events.


# Fixed
=========

-> Client list not updating correctly
Now updates on connect, disconnect, and kick events.

-> Incorrect GUI title before display name was set
Title now updates after the client successfully connects.

-> Multiple /userList parsing issues
Consolidated into a single, reliable handler.

-> Server not closing cleanly on window exit
Now shuts down all clients and closes the socket properly.


# Removed
===========

-> Deprecated or unused code from the original version, including:
Old console‑only server dashboard.
Unused variables and commented‑out sections.
Legacy ExampleChatServer references.
